<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amorite Wall</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as defensive wall constructed to repel Amorites</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Amorite Wall was a defensive wall built by kings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> to keep out Amorite groups migrating from the west. It was constructed in the late third millennium BCE across the land north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumer">Sumer</a>. Its failure to stop Amorite incursions illustrates the pressures that contributed to the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-sumerian-empire">Neo-Sumerian Empire</a>.</p></div>
